+# Playwright perf-budget gate ΓÇö MovementsScreen
+
+> **Issue:** #39-c ┬╖ **Owner:** Cypher ┬╖ **Priority:** P0
+
+## What this gate does
+
+A Playwright test (`tests/e2e/movements-perf.spec.ts`) launches the real Electron
+binary against a seeded 5 000-transaction dataset and measures how long it takes
+for the first data row to become visible in the Movements screen after clicking
+the nav item.
+
+The test runs **3 independent Electron launches** and asserts that the **median
+mount time is Γëñ 500 ms**.  Using the median rather than the minimum absorbs
+single-run cold-start noise without hiding a genuine regression across all runs.
+
+CI only triggers this job on **pushes to `main`** (not on PRs) ΓÇö see *Revisiting
+the gate* below.
+
+---
+
+## Budget rationale
+
+| Threshold | Reasoning |
+|-----------|-----------|
+| **500 ms** | Starting point calibrated to the post-virtualisation (#39-a) expected median. Once stable, tune to `observed_median ├ù 1.5` to give a safety margin without flaking on cold runners. |
+| 3 runs | Enough for a stable median on CI runners; keeps the job under ~5 min. |
+
+The 500 ms budget is intentionally conservative for the first landing.  After a
+week of data from real CI runs, adjust it to `median ├ù 1.5` so it gates genuine
+regressions while remaining flake-resistant on slow runners.
+
+**Why not P50 across more runs?**  Each run spawns a full Electron process, which
+takes 3ΓÇô10 s per launch on CI.  Three runs keep the job manageable; more runs can
+be added if the variance turns out to be high.
+
+---
+
+## How to reproduce locally
+
+```bash
+# 1. Build the app (renderer + main + preload).
+npm run build
+
+# 2. Install Playwright (only needed once).
+npx playwright install
+
+# 3. Seed 5 000 synthetic transactions.
+npm run perf:seed -- --count=5000 --dir=perf-events
+
+# 4. Run the perf spec only.
+npx playwright test movements-perf
+
+# Run the full e2e suite (smoke + perf):
+npm run e2e
+```
+
+---
+
+## Debugging a CI failure
+
+### 1 ΓÇö Read the median and individual run times
+
+The test prints each run time and the median to stdout:
+
+```
+[perf] run 1/3: 312 ms
+[perf] run 2/3: 289 ms
+[perf] run 3/3: 418 ms
+[perf] times=[289, 312, 418] ms  median=312 ms  budget=500 ms
+```
+
+If the median exceeds 500 ms, look for **all three runs** being slow (genuine
+regression) versus **one outlier** inflating the median (runner flakiness).
+
+### 2 ΓÇö Check for a renderer regression
+
+The #1 suspect is a change that un-virtualises the Movements table or forces a
+full DOM re-render.  Confirm by:
+
+```bash
+# Local measurement with React DevTools Profiler:
+npm run dev
+# Open DevTools ΓåÆ Profiler ΓåÆ record ΓåÆ click Movimientos
+```
+
+Check `Table.tsx` ΓÇö the `virtualise` prop must be `true` for the Movements
+table (see `MovementsScreen.tsx`).
+
+### 3 ΓÇö Check for a data-layer regression
+
+Run the data-layer harness to isolate main-process cost:
+
+```bash
+npm run perf:measure -- --sizes=5000 --trials=5
+```
+
+Expected at 5 000 rows (post #39-b fix): **Γëñ 80 ms** total main-process cost
+(`load` + `replayEvents` + `movements:list` + `zod.parse`).
+
+### 4 ΓÇö Check the seed
+
+Confirm the perf-events dataset exists and has the right size:
+
+```bash
+# Linux / macOS
+ls -lh ~/.config/opentreasury-desktop/perf-events/events.ndjson
+
+# Windows
+dir %APPDATA%\opentreasury-desktop\perf-events\events.ndjson
+```
+
+A 5 000-transaction seed (+ reference data) is ~3.5 MiB.
+
+---
+
+## Revisiting the gate
+
+After ΓëÑ 1 week of stable data on `main`:
+
+1. Collect the median values logged by CI runs.
+2. Compute `p75 ├ù 1.5` from the collected medians.
+3. Update `BUDGET_MS` in `tests/e2e/movements-perf.spec.ts`.
+4. If variance is low (all runs within ┬▒20 ms of the median), change the CI
+   `if:` condition to also fire on PRs ΓÇö edit `.github/workflows/ci.yml` and
+   remove the `github.event_name == 'push'` guard.
+
+---
+
+## Related
+
+- `tests/e2e/movements-perf.spec.ts` ΓÇö the gate itself
+- `playwright.config.ts` ΓÇö Playwright project config (timeout, retries)
+- `scripts/perf-seed.mjs` ΓÇö deterministic 5 k-transaction seed
+- `docs/perf/movements-investigation-2026-04-24.md` ΓÇö root-cause analysis
+- Issue #39-a (virtualisation) ΓÇö prerequisite for the budget to be meetable
